webhooks.gleam: `corrected ->
  // ISO timestamps — lexical compare is chronological.
  string.compare(at, corrected) != order.Lt` — `at` is RFC3339 (sweep.gleam:179-180 `timestamp.to_rfc3339(calendar.utc_offset)`, e.g. '2026-08-12T08:00:00Z') while `corrected_at` is `COALESCE(rc.corrected_at::text, '')` (Postgres '2026-08-12 10:00:00+00', space separator): at position 10 'T'(0x54) > ' '(0x20), so a same-day pre-correction send compares GREATER than the correction and is misclassified genuine. Tests pin only the cross-day case (send '2026-08-01T08:00:00Z' vs corrected_at=real now) where the date digits decide.

form_handler.gleam: `to_email: effective(row.corrected_email, row.contact_email),
      to_phone: effective(row.corrected_phone, row.contact_phone),` and `fn effective(
  corrected: Option(String),
  snapshot: Option(String),
) -> Option(String) {
  case corrected, snapshot {
    Some(c), _ -> Some(c)` — no `correction_cycles >= 1` gate (unlike sweep.gleam:712 `case row.correction_cycles >= 1 { True -> row.corrected_email ...}`).
